<LLMTokenQuota name="LTQ-Enforce" continueOnError="false" enabled="true">
  <DisplayName>LLM Token Quota Tier 2 -- one department within this use case (enforce)</DisplayName>
  <Operation>EnforceOnly</Operation>
  <!--
    RE-PURPOSED 2026-09-17 as Tier 2 of quota(use case, LTQ-App-*) x
    quota(department within it, HERE) x quota(user within that department,
    LTQ-User-*). Previously the ONLY token check on this proxy, Identified
    by llm_user_department alone (one shared 25,000,000/hour ceiling per
    department, across all three use cases combined).

    Re-keyed to llm_dept_app (department:client_id, already computed by
    AM-Identity.xml for PTL-PromptTokenLimit) and switched OFF
    UseQuotaConfigInAPIProduct — that mechanism is now Tier 1's
    (LTQ-App-Enforce.xml reads the product's one llmQuota field so every use
    case gets its own full 25,000,000/hour). Tier 2 needs its own, smaller,
    genuinely-nested number, so it reads a product ATTRIBUTE instead,
    the same Allow/countRef shape as every plain Quota policy elsewhere in
    this codebase. See LTQ-User-Enforce.xml's comment on this being the
    first exercise of that element combination on an LLMTokenQuota policy —
    unverified against a live deploy.
  -->
  <Allow count="10000000" countRef="verifyapikey.VA-ApiKey.apiproduct.llm_tokens_per_hour_dept"/>
  <Interval>1</Interval>
  <TimeUnit>hour</TimeUnit>
  <Identifier ref="llm_dept_app"/>
  <LLMModelSource>{llm.model}</LLMModelSource>
  <!--
    Required even in EnforceOnly. Omitting it does NOT mean there is no usage source:
    the policy falls back to a response-based default and evaluates it in the
    REQUEST flow, where no response exists yet, so every call died with

      500 entities.UnresolvedVariable
      "Unresolved variable : response.content"   (state=PROXY_REQ_FLOW)

    Confirmed from an Apigee debug session 2026-09-15: every prior policy
    passed and this one reported result=false. See docs/BUILD-LOG.md #39.

    The value is a literal 0 because this instance only CHECKS the counter
    before the call; it must add nothing to it. The actual token count is
    recorded by LTQ-Count in the response flow, which is where the real usage
    figure exists.
  -->
  <LLMTokenUsageSource>0</LLMTokenUsageSource>
</LLMTokenQuota>
